.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-REVOKE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-revoke
.Nd say that a seal key must no longer be trusted
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis revoke
.Fl k Ar key
.Op Fl p Ar key.pub
.Op Fl -at Ar time
.Op Fl -reason Ar text
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Fl f
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis revoke
writes a key statement
.Pq Ql noqtis-keys-1 , Xr noqtis-capsule 5 ,
signed by
.Ar key ,
that it is revoked from
.Ar time ,
for instance because it may have been copied.
.Xr noqtis-check 1
.Fl -keys Ar file
then accepts a capsule sealed with
.Ar key
only when a verified timestamp
.Pq Fl -anchor
shows that it was sealed before
.Ar time :
the manifest's
.Ql created
is the sealer's own word, and a thief holding the key could write any.
Make the statement while you still hold the key, and keep a copy apart
from it.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl k Ar key , Fl -key Ns = Ns Ar key
The secret key being revoked.
.It Fl p Ar key.pub , Fl -pub Ns = Ns Ar key.pub
Its public key.
Default:
.Ar key Ns Pa .pub .
.It Fl -at Ar time
When the revocation takes effect, as
.Ql YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ
(UTC, 1970 or later).
Default: now.
.It Fl -reason Ar text
Up to 255 bytes of text, kept in the statement.
.It Fl o Ar file , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar file
Write the statement to
.Ar file
instead of standard output.
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace
.Ar file
if it exists.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 3n -compact
.It 0
The statement was written.
.It 2
A usage error, a key file that cannot be read, a key that is not a
post-quantum signature key pair, or a file that cannot be written.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis revoke -k me --reason "laptop lost" -o me.revoked
$ noqtis check -p me.pub --anchor tsa-root.der --keys me.revoked results
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-rotate 1 ,
.Xr nqkstmt 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
